WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.552
The fictional installation package
contains the user requirements,

2
00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:07.430
design-review outcome, accepted drawings

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.550
and an installation protocol.

4
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.188
List identifiers and revisions before the
walkdown.

5
00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:15.889
An email attachment labelled final is

6
00:00:16.009 --> 00:00:19.043
not enough to establish its approval
status.

7
00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:23.922
If the valve drawing changed after design
review, identify the change

8
00:00:24.042 --> 00:00:28.249
and its accepted impact before relying on
the old conclusion.

9
00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:32.731
Replace verify installation is
satisfactory with a check

10
00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:35.196
another trained person can repeat.

11
00:00:35.316 --> 00:00:38.833
For example, compare the installed outlet
valve tag

12
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:41.574
and model against schedule revision C,

13
00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:43.763
using a safe visual inspection

14
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:46.504
and the identified manufacturer plate.

15
00:00:46.624 --> 00:00:49.382
Define what information will be recorded

16
00:00:49.502 --> 00:00:52.675
and how inaccessible markings will be
handled.

17
00:00:52.795 --> 00:00:57.760
Do not leave the acceptance rule to be
invented after seeing the result.

18
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.242
Before inspecting, confirm training,
access arrangements

19
00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:06.845
and any required isolation with the
responsible engineering team.

20
00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:10.965
Do not remove guards, open electrical
panels or disconnect

21
00:01:11.085 --> 00:01:14.257
a process line merely to complete a
checklist.

22
00:01:14.377 --> 00:01:16.998
If a marking cannot be reached safely,

23
00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:20.842
record that limitation and arrange an
approved method.

24
00:01:20.962 --> 00:01:23.790
Schedule pressure does not turn an unsafe

25
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.393
inspection into acceptable evidence.

26
00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:29.564
Suppose the drawing shows a clearance

27
00:01:29.684 --> 00:01:31.960
but provides no approved minimum.

28
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.218
Measuring a convenient distance

29
00:01:34.338 --> 00:01:38.407
and then calling it acceptable creates a
circular argument.

30
00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:41.838
Raise the missing requirement to the
responsible

31
00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.958
design and quality functions.

32
00:01:44.078 --> 00:01:47.802
The team may collect a clearly identified
observation,

33
00:01:47.922 --> 00:01:52.681
but acceptance of that feature remains
unresolved until the criterion

34
00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.421
and approach are properly established.
